# L §5 A form defined by another (tally 2.1.7 R6, issue #145; T's SR-7): next(K, d) is first(m in K over d ..) ties by
# m.day, and "gives its values, holes and refusals, their messages naming the form as written". gift and gift2 fall on
# one day: RUN-TIE naming next(transfers, d1) (n_tie_next); after both, HOLE-NOTYET naming next(transfers, after_all)
# (n_none). 2.1.7's first refcore named the definition's bound m and the day's value, next(transfers, 2026-03-02).
=== sr7.tally
model sr7
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "T's card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input fee: money PLN

input late: date

input d1: date

input after_all: date

move gift2: transfers
  on late
  leg cash from world to konto amount fee

move gift: transfers
  on late
  leg cash from world to konto amount fee

ask n_tie_next: next(transfers, d1)

ask n_none: next(transfers, after_all)

version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  fee = ?"how much is the gift?"
  late = 2026-06-10 "after the cut"
  d1 = 2026-03-02 "after the cut"
  after_all = 2026-07-01 "after both gifts"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
=== expect
n_none: ?"next(transfers, after_all): no transfers yet, and its span reaches past the cut" (transfers)
  cut 2026-03-01
n_tie_next: refused: RUN-TIE next(transfers, d1) has a tie at gift, gift2 that changes the result, and its ties by doesn't break it
  cut 2026-03-01
